Interpretation
Consider two competing values of \theta for observing x=2 heads in n=2 tosses:

If \theta=0.01, the probability of observing X=2 is 
  L(0.01;2)=0.0001.
   For such a coin, two heads would be highly unusual.
If \theta=0.99, the probability of observing X=2 is 
